From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jean-Michael Celerier <jmcelerier@sat.qc.ca>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 10:53:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] rhi: vulkan: offscreen render passes wait for previous
 attachment writes

createOffscreenRenderPass() gave a texture render target's render pass
no external subpass dependency, leaving the barriers to the resource
tracking. Those barriers end at the attachment stages, but an attachment
whose contents are not preserved starts the pass from
VK_IMAGE_LAYOUT_UNDEFINED, and that layout transition happens at the
start of the external dependency. With only the implicit dependency
(TOP_OF_PIPE, no access) the transition does not chain after the
barrier, so two passes into the same texture render target within one
command buffer race: the second pass's layout transition against the
first pass's color and depth writes. The synchronization validation
layer reports SYNC-HAZARD-WRITE-AFTER-WRITE at vkCmdBeginRenderPass for
every color and depth attachment.

Add an external dependency from the attachment stages and writes, which
chains with the tracking barriers.
---
 src/gui/rhi/qrhivulkan.cpp | 28 ++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/gui/rhi/qrhivulkan.cpp b/src/gui/rhi/qrhivulkan.cpp
index f3f615d1f337..3328dfafc712 100644
--- a/src/gui/rhi/qrhivulkan.cpp
+++ b/src/gui/rhi/qrhivulkan.cpp
@@ -2271,10 +2271,30 @@ bool QRhiVulkan::createOffscreenRenderPass(QVkRenderPassDescriptor *rpD,
     selfDependency.dependencyFlags = depFlags;
     rpD->subpassDeps.append(selfDependency);
 
-    // rpD->subpassDeps stays empty: don't yet know the correct initial/final
-    // access and stage stuff for the implicit deps at this point, so leave it
-    // to the resource tracking and activateTextureRenderTarget() to generate
-    // barriers.
+    // The resource tracking and activateTextureRenderTarget() put a barrier
+    // before the pass for whatever last used its attachments. That barrier
+    // ends at the attachment stages, while an attachment whose contents are
+    // not preserved starts from VK_IMAGE_LAYOUT_UNDEFINED, and that layout
+    // transition happens at the start of the external dependency. With only
+    // the implicit one (TOP_OF_PIPE, no access) the transition does not
+    // chain after the barrier and races the writes a previous pass made to
+    // the same image: two passes into one texture render target in a command
+    // buffer were a write-after-write hazard. Make the dependency start at
+    // the attachment stages so it chains.
+    VkSubpassDependency externalDep = {};
+    externalDep.srcSubpass = VK_SUBPASS_EXTERNAL;
+    externalDep.dstSubpass = 0;
+    externalDep.srcStageMask = VK_PIPELINE_STAGE_COLOR_ATTACHMENT_OUTPUT_BIT
+                             | VK_PIPELINE_STAGE_EARLY_FRAGMENT_TESTS_BIT
+                             | VK_PIPELINE_STAGE_LATE_FRAGMENT_TESTS_BIT;
+    externalDep.dstStageMask = externalDep.srcStageMask;
+    externalDep.srcAccessMask = VK_ACCESS_COLOR_ATTACHMENT_WRITE_BIT
+                              | VK_ACCESS_DEPTH_STENCIL_ATTACHMENT_WRITE_BIT;
+    externalDep.dstAccessMask = VK_ACCESS_COLOR_ATTACHMENT_READ_BIT
+                              | VK_ACCESS_COLOR_ATTACHMENT_WRITE_BIT
+                              | VK_ACCESS_DEPTH_STENCIL_ATTACHMENT_READ_BIT
+                              | VK_ACCESS_DEPTH_STENCIL_ATTACHMENT_WRITE_BIT;
+    rpD->subpassDeps.append(externalDep);
 
     VkRenderPassCreateInfo rpInfo;
     VkSubpassDescription subpassDesc;
